  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sphere of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\; \\textup{m}\"></span> is rotating about its diameter with an angular speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\; \\textup{rad\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>. The moment of inertia for the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{2}{5}mr^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is the radius of the sphere.</p>\n<p>Given that the rotational kinetic energy of the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\\; \\textup{J}\"></span>, what is the mass of the sphere?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.5\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
